# TestKotlinVsJavaFernflower: fernflower's main set analysed twice, as Java and as its J2K translation to Kotlin
# (maddi-run-analysis's j2k/fernflower-nullability output), with the same configuration otherwise. Two-sided, as
# CensusRatchet: a line that is new fails (a regression, or a change to record deliberately), and a recorded line that
# is gone fails too (an improvement: remove it in the commit that earns it). The test writes the actual lines to
# build/kotlin-vs-java/fernflower/fernflower.ratchet.actual.
#
# Recorded: the per-side numbers, each kind's summary (the naming categories, accessors, companions, ..., by count
# only), then every element of a category that judges a verdict: kotlin-weaker (precision the Kotlin side lost),
# kotlin-stronger (Kotlin claims more than Java: a soundness question, maddi-mod#145), kotlin-none/java-none,
# differ (types), java-only and kotlin-only-other. A verdict is true for unmodified (F, P) or non-modifying (M).
#
# 2026-11-19, first record: maddi a2cc271ff (with the forEach lowering, 92e523553 + d81b290e3), maddi-mod f3531e77,
# run on the Mac. Known: appendTypeParameters#3 kotlin-weaker is a Java gap (maddi-mod#138); the ConstExprent maps and
# ClassWriter.MODIFIERS kotlin-stronger are Java counting its static initializer as a modification.
#
# 2026-11-19, re-recorded with the reachability pass on (RunMixedPrepAnalyzer.Options.reachability; maddi 7ef10cdf6,
# maddi-mod fb286554), as the analysis engine and the IDE daemon run: the first record had the fixpoint verdicts only.
# Types differ 4 -> 1, kotlin-stronger F 10 -> 4, M 8 -> 7, P 18 -> 15; kotlin-weaker M 11 -> 15, P 6 -> 8. With
# -Dmaddi.kotlinVsJava.culprits=true the run writes explain.txt, both sides' culprits per differing verdict.
#
# 2026-11-19, maddi b4ceaf52c (`e.also { v = it }` is Java's `(v = e)`) and f5a904b10 (an object expression's members
# capture the enclosing parameters): kotlin-stronger M 7 -> 6, P 15 -> 8. Gone: both getMaxBreakLift, the
# DirectGraph.ExprentIterator chain (iterateExprents, StatementIterator.iterate, updateVersions).
#
# 2026-11-20, maddi 79ee97c86 (J2K's `run sw@ { … return@sw … }` is the labelled block `sw: { … break sw; … }`) and
# 7a609ac06 (`m.values` typed at the use site, Collection<U>): kotlin-stronger F 4 -> 2, M 6 -> 3, P 8 -> 6. Gone:
# ExprProcessor.processBlock/processStatement, FlattenStatementsHelper.StackEntry.finally*RangeSource,
# StructContext.saveContext. getTypeName, writeNestedClass and listToJava stay: Java is right only because it
# reassigns its own parameter; both sides lose a copied list's elements (#138 stream form, #152 loop form).
#
# 2026-11-20, maddi 92db37125 (an `object :` declares all its methods before their bodies: `return r(e)` lost its
# call) and ecff95f88 (an `object :`'s property initializers capture the enclosing locals): kotlin-stronger
# F 2 -> 1, M 3 -> 2, P 6 -> 4. Gone: ClassNode.superInvocation, ExprentIteratorWithReplace.processExprent (M, P),
# NestedClassProcessor.iterateExprents#1. StackVarsProcessor.replaceSingleVar#3, which Java gained with #147, stays
# in agreement. MethodProcessorRunnable.root stays: Java links root to the StructMethod handed to the same
# MethodProcessorRunnable; neither MethodWrapper.root nor .methodStruct is modified on either side.

